DATA:
    Data = information that we want to store and use
    · e.g. users, names, emails, products, prices, orders, payments
    . Data can exist in different forms: numbers, text, dates, images, etc
    · In an application, data is continuously created, read, updated, and deleted
    . As the application grows, managing large amounts of data becomes difficult

// ab is data ko muje relibaly organised way & relibaly fast retrive krna h to we use database

Database
· A database is an organized system for storing and managing data
· It provides persistent storage for application data
· Allows us to efficiently create, read, update, and delete data
. Databases can handle large amounts of data and many concurrent users
· A relational database organizes data into tables consisting of rows and columns
. Tables can be connected through relationships
· Examples of relational databases: PostgreSQL, MySQL, Oracle, SQL Server, SQLite
. The software that manages a database is called a DBMS (Database Management System)

 Application -----> Need all users------>DBMS (Postgres)----->Fetches users from disk----->disk

SQL
  SELECT * FROM users;
. SQL = Structured Query Language
· SQL is a language used to communicate with relational databases
· It allows us to create, read, update, and delete data
· SQL can also be used to define tables, relationships, constraints, indexes, etc.
. SQL is primarily a declarative language we tell the database what we want,
   not exactly how to get it
. Different database systems may have their own SQL extensions and syntax

  SELECT *
* FROM users WHERE age > 23: